# Next.js 15 App Router Patterns

## App Router Structure
- Use Next.js 15 App Router with React 19
- Server components by default, client components when needed
- Colocate page, layout, loading, and error files
- Use route groups for organization: `(auth)`, `(chat)`, etc.

## Development Commands
- **Dev**: `pnpm dev --turbopack` (with Turbopack for faster builds)
- **Build**: `pnpm build --turbopack`
- **Start**: `pnpm start`

## Component Patterns
- Server components for data fetching and static content
- Client components for interactivity (`'use client'` directive)
- Use React 19 features: concurrent features, automatic batching, transitions
- Implement proper loading states with `loading.tsx` files
- Create error boundaries with `error.tsx` files

## Route Protection
- Implement authentication guards for protected routes
- Redirect unauthenticated users to login
- Use middleware for route-level protection when needed
- Server actions for authenticated operations

## Data Fetching
- Use server components for initial data loading
- Client-side Firebase listeners for real-time updates
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Use React Suspense boundaries appropriately

## Performance Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized images
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting
- Optimize bundle size with tree shaking

## Routing Conventions
- `page.tsx`: Route pages
- `layout.tsx`: Shared layouts
- `loading.tsx`: Loading UI
- `error.tsx`: Error boundaries
- `not-found.tsx`: 404 pages
- `route.ts`: API routes (if needed)

## Server Actions
- Use server actions for form handling and mutations
- Implement proper validation and error handling
- Keep server actions focused and single-purpose
- Use proper TypeScript types for action parameters